window.docContents[75].resolve({"/Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols/L1-___-Two-bodies/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L1-___-Two-bodies--Synopsis--Errors-prevented":{"contents":"* Cross-system contamination: oscillator B's mass used in oscillator A's k/m. Bare reals and Quantity values without a bearer accept it; IndividualQuantity rejects it with a type mismatch (HCP.L1_TwoBodies#bare_real_cross_oscillators, HCP.L1_TwoBodies#kinded_bearer_free_cross_oscillators, HCP.L1_TwoBodies#refused_cross_oscillator).* False identity: one name used for both oscillators, so A and B are reported as one system. The designation_inj proof that every Designated instance needs rules this out (HCP.L1_TwoBodies#designation).* Unsorted bearer: a quantity about an object of no stated sort. It fails to type-check because no Sorted instance exists for the object's type (HCP.L1_TwoBodies#refused_unsorted_object).\n\n","context":"A Property Kind Calculus for Metrology: proving quantity and unit laws in Lean, from ISO/IEC 80000 to measurement uncertainty\u0009Onboarding: Human Context Protocols\u0009L1 — Two bodies\u0009Synopsis","header":"5.2.1.4. Errors prevented","id":"/Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols/L1-___-Two-bodies/#A-Property-Kind-Calculus-for-Metrology___-proving-quantity-and-unit-laws-in-Lean___-from-ISO___IEC-80000-to-measurement-uncertainty--Onboarding___-Human-Context-Protocols--L1-___-Two-bodies--Synopsis--Errors-prevented"}});